  "title": "Ukraine and Russia: Aerial Attacks Escalate as US Envoys Revisit Moscow",
  "summary": "A heavy Russian missile and drone bombardment has killed at least 15 people in and around Kyiv, with Ukrainian intelligence units describing a 'disgraceful' shootout. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrive in Moscow to try to revive peace talks, while Russia plans a 72-hour pause in strikes on Kyiv.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "A heavy Russian missile and drone bombardment has killed at least 15 people in and around Kyiv in one of the most intense aerial attacks on Ukraine’s capital since the start of the war.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy described the shootout in Kyiv as an 'absolutely disgraceful' event.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Russian President Vladimir Putin ordered a 72-hour pause in Kyiv strikes, starting at midnight today, as US envoys arrive in Moscow to try to revive peace talks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
